'''arret<sup>2</sup>†''' (a-rā′ or a-ret′), ''n.'' [< F. ''arrêt'', < OF. ''arest'', arrest: see ''arrest''<sup>1</sup>, ''n.''] The decision of a court, tribunal, or council; a decree published; the edict of a sovereign prince: applied to the judgments and decisions of courts and tribunals in France.

